; Interrupt vector table for IM 2: 257 bytes of $85
;
; With I = $84 (set by #R$6000) the CPU reads the vector from $84xx, where xx is whatever the data bus carries during
; the interrupt acknowledge ($FF on a Spectrum, but not guaranteed). All 257 bytes are $85, so every vector is $8585,
; the interrupt handler #R$8585 (the table is one byte longer than a page so that the vector for $FF, read from $84FF
; and $8500, is also $8585).
; .
; Hardware: read by the CPU during the 50 Hz frame interrupt.
@label=Im2Table
b$8400 DEFS $0101,$85
